WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.432 --> 00:00:04.015
(hinge creaks)

00:00:05.096 --> 00:00:06.579
- Hi, I'm Adriane Kruer.

00:00:06.579 --> 00:00:09.031
I'm a clinical psychologist
in Los Angeles.

00:00:09.031 --> 00:00:11.963
I've been working with kids and
families for about 10 years.

00:00:11.963 --> 00:00:15.223
I am a licensed psychologist working

00:00:15.223 --> 00:00:17.159
with children ages three to 18.

00:00:17.159 --> 00:00:18.905
I started working with children

00:00:18.905 --> 00:00:20.828
when I did a master's in art therapy.

00:00:20.828 --> 00:00:22.815
I really love working with families

00:00:22.815 --> 00:00:24.735
to help them understand their kids better,

00:00:24.735 --> 00:00:25.570
communicate better,

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.799
and get along better with
their friends and family.

00:00:27.799 --> 00:00:30.314
So some of the signs of
depression in children

00:00:30.314 --> 00:00:32.115
might be not wanting to do things

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:33.589
that they normally like to do,

00:00:33.589 --> 00:00:36.099
like they don't wanna go to
their normal soccer practice,

00:00:36.099 --> 00:00:38.097
they might not want to go to a sleepover

00:00:38.097 --> 00:00:39.632
and they normally would really like that.

00:00:39.632 --> 00:00:41.238
Another thing that kids might show

00:00:41.238 --> 00:00:43.882
when they're feeling depressed
is some bodily symptoms.

00:00:43.882 --> 00:00:45.956
They might have headaches more often,

00:00:45.956 --> 00:00:47.528
maybe more stomachaches.

00:00:47.528 --> 00:00:49.996
They might go to the
nurse's office more often.

00:00:49.996 --> 00:00:51.481
They might also have trouble getting along

00:00:51.481 --> 00:00:54.609
with other kids at school
or with their siblings.

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:56.420
You might hear about
this at a school meeting.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.729
Kids might also be a
little more irritable.

00:00:58.729 --> 00:01:00.759
Maybe they have more outbursts.

00:01:00.759 --> 00:01:03.239
You might notice that
they're a little more angry

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:04.683
than they normally would be.

00:01:04.683 --> 00:01:06.134
That would definitely be a sign

00:01:06.134 --> 00:01:08.648
that they're having some
sort of sadness going on.

00:01:08.648 --> 00:01:11.008
When talking with your
kids about their feelings,

00:01:11.008 --> 00:01:12.556
it is really important to let them know

00:01:12.556 --> 00:01:14.517
that you are safe to talk to,

00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:16.175
that you can be there for them.

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:18.639
Kids when they're feeling
sad might not understand

00:01:18.639 --> 00:01:19.940
that they feel depressed.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.790
They may not know what's
really going on for them.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.175
So it's really important as adults

00:01:23.175 --> 00:01:25.909
that we provide a really
safe space for them to talk.

00:01:25.909 --> 00:01:28.986
We might want to give
them a lot of reassurance

00:01:28.986 --> 00:01:32.346
and provide them some
encouragement to open up.

00:01:32.346 --> 00:01:35.613
If you do have concerns
that your child is in danger

00:01:35.613 --> 00:01:37.065
or they may have thoughts

00:01:37.065 --> 00:01:38.702
of hurting themselves or someone else,

00:01:38.702 --> 00:01:41.145
it is important to reach
out for help right away.

00:01:41.145 --> 00:01:41.978
Don't wait.

00:01:41.978 --> 00:01:44.706
So you can call your local
emergency services, 911,

00:01:44.706 --> 00:01:46.081
or the suicide hotline.

00:01:46.081 --> 00:01:47.698
They do have a youth division.

00:01:47.698 --> 00:01:50.270
Paying attention to
feelings is really important

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:53.718
to understand how we are
getting along in the world

00:01:53.718 --> 00:01:55.301
with ourselves and with other people.

00:01:55.301 --> 00:01:57.743
Reaching out to a professional
can be a great way

00:01:57.743 --> 00:01:59.162
to just start the conversation.

00:01:59.162 --> 00:02:01.552
Kids can make a lot of
progress in therapy.

00:02:01.552 --> 00:02:03.825
They can really start to understand

00:02:03.825 --> 00:02:07.009
who they are as people, even
when they're very little,

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:08.669
so it's nice for them to have a space

00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:10.299
where they can get to know themselves,

00:02:10.299 --> 00:02:13.189
start to understand how
they wanna be in the world.

00:02:13.189 --> 00:02:15.772
(bright music)

